# Formatting for port/ ONLY. Never applied to module/, which is the recompiler's output and is compared byte for byte
# by the preservation track; reformatting it would destroy that comparison.
#
# This file is written to match the style port/ already uses rather than to change it: tabs, 4-wide, braces attached,
# 120 columns, trailing comments left aligned in their column. It was first run on 2026-11-03, in a commit of its own as
# this note asked, and version 18 is the one that counts: CI has clang-format 18 and 19 disagrees with it on
# access-modifier indent and pointer alignment, so running a newer one reformats the tree into a state the gate rejects.
# The pin is therefore the clang-format major, and `python3 -m venv` plus `pip install clang-format==18.1.8` is how to
# get exactly it without a distro package manager deciding for you.
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
Language: Cpp
UseTab: Always
IndentWidth: 4
TabWidth: 4
ColumnLimit: 120
BreakBeforeBraces: Attach
AlignTrailingComments: true
SpacesBeforeTrailingComments: 2
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: Never
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: InlineOnly
SortIncludes: false
